---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Comments from '../../components/Comments.astro';
import RegionMap from '../../components/RegionMap.astro';
const P = 'https://media.huanyuchen.com/misc/cat-cafes/';
const L = (label, lat, lon) => ({ label, lat, lon });
const SPOTS = [
  { name: "Miko's Pet Supplies", locs: [L('West Covina', 34.0489, -117.9067)] },
  { name: 'Fika Fika (adoption days)', locs: [L('Arcadia', 34.13131, -118.06662)] },
  { name: 'Save The Meow Meows Cat Lounge', locs: [L('Yucca Valley', 34.1202, -116.4223)] },
  { name: 'Whiskers & Wine', locs: [L('San Diego', 32.7629, -117.1325)] },
];
const AWAY = [
  { name: 'Brooklyn Cat Cafe', locs: [L('Brooklyn Heights', 40.69522, -73.9964)] },
];
const PLACES = [
  { name: 'Ernest Hemingway Home', locs: [L('Key West', 24.5512, -81.8006)] },
  { name: 'Hilton Waikoloa Village self-parking lot', locs: [L('Waikoloa', 19.9221, -155.8884)] },
];
const BAY = [
  { name: 'Mini Cat Town', locs: [L('Palo Alto', 37.42603, -122.14484)] },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Cat Cafés — Huanyu Chen"
  description="Cats we did not take home, 2023–2026: Brooklyn Cat Cafe on New Year's Day, the cat room at Miko's Pet Supplies in West Covina, kitten adoption days at Fika Fika in Arcadia, a cat lounge in Yucca Valley, a cat wine bar in San Diego, Mini Cat Town in Palo Alto, the Hemingway cats of Key West, a parking lot full of cats in Waikoloa, and the kittens we fostered in 2023, with maps.">
  <p class="muted"><a href="/misc">← Misc</a> · 2023 – 2026</p>
  <h1>Cat Cafés</h1>
  <p class="muted trip-sub">Cats we visited but did not take home, and a few we did, for a while.</p>

  <div class="callout trip-stats">
    <strong>4 years · January 2023 – October 2026</strong><br />
    a cat asleep in a carrot in Brooklyn · a calico asleep on a lap · a tuxedo cat upside down · an orange kitten in a denim jacket · kittens in pens next to a
    lavender ice cream · a black cat in Yucca Valley · a cat lounge with a wine bar · kittens in Palo Alto · a six-toed welcome in Key West · dozens of cats in a Hawaiʻi parking lot · three rounds of foster kittens
  </div>

  <p>
    Most of these photos are from my wife's camera roll; the Brooklyn and Palo Alto ones are stills from our videos. They are the places where the cats belong to someone
    else, or are waiting for someone: a cat café in Brooklyn, a pet store with a cat room, adoption days at a café, three cat lounges, and two places where the cats simply live. At the end are the kittens we fostered in 2023.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={SPOTS} region="Southern California" />

  <h2 id="miko">Miko's Pet Supplies, West Covina</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Miko's Pet Supplies</strong> in West Covina has a room full of cats, with shelves and scratching posts up the
    walls. In 2024 it was the regular stop, ten times by the card records between May and the next January. In May
    there was a calico who fell asleep on a lap.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'miko-calico.webp'} alt="A calico cat curled up asleep on someone's lap." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Asleep, Miko's, May 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'miko-shelf.webp'} alt="Two black-and-white cats stretched out asleep on a wall shelf." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Two on a shelf, September 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In September, a tuxedo cat who would only lie upside down, and in December an orange kitten that fit inside a
    denim jacket.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'miko-tuxedo.webp'} alt="A black-and-white cat lying upside down across a lap in jeans, paws in the air." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Upside down, September 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'miko-kitten.webp'} alt="An orange-and-white kitten peeking out from inside a denim jacket." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>In the jacket, December 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="fika">Adoption days at Fika Fika, Arcadia</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Fika Fika</strong>, the Arcadia café from the sweets post, hosts adoption days with
    <strong>Cat and Comics Rescue</strong>: pens of kittens to look at with a coffee or an ice cream
    in hand.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'fika-icecream.webp'} alt="A hand holding a lavender ice cream cone in front of wire pens of kittens." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Ice cream and kittens, Fika Fika, May 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'fika-kittens.webp'} alt="Kittens piled together inside a wire pen on blue blankets." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A pen of kittens, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In July 2023 there was a gray-and-white longhair kitten, and a black kitten who had settled into the litter box.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'fika-gray-kitten.webp'} alt="A fluffy gray-and-white kitten held up close to the camera." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The longhair, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'fika-black-kitten.webp'} alt="A black kitten lying in a box of wood-pellet litter inside a pen." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>In the litter box.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="lounges">Two cat lounges</h2>
  <p>
    The evening we arrived for a Joshua Tree weekend in December 2024, we went to <strong>Save The Meow Meows Cat
    Lounge</strong> in Yucca Valley, where a big black cat settled onto a lap. Later that night was
    <a href="/misc/joshua-tree#dec-2024">Orion over the Joshua trees</a>.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'meow-black-cat.webp'} alt="A large black cat lying across a lap, being petted." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Save The Meow Meows Cat Lounge, Yucca Valley, December 8, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    And in October 2026, <strong>Whiskers &amp; Wine</strong> on Adams Avenue in San Diego, a cocktail bar with a cat
    lounge.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'whiskers-lounge.webp'} alt="A cat lounge with wall shelves, a gold mirror and cat beds, a black-and-white cat on a leopard-print rug." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Whiskers &amp; Wine, San Diego, October 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'whiskers-cat.webp'} alt="A tabby cat by the glass door of the lounge, next to a water bowl." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>By the door.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mini-cat-town">Mini Cat Town, Palo Alto</h2>
  <p>
    One evening in August 2026 was at <strong>Mini Cat Town</strong> on California Avenue in Palo Alto, a cat lounge
    run by a rescue, where the cats are up for adoption and shoe covers go on at the door. The Siamese-point kittens
    took the sofa: one stretched out under a hand, one sat up for a chin scratch.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'minicat-siamese.webp'} alt="A cream kitten with dark points stretched out on a gray sofa, a hand beside it." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On the sofa, Mini Cat Town, August 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'minicat-chin.webp'} alt="A cream kitten with dark points sitting up on the sofa for a chin scratch." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Sitting up.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    A black cat claimed a white chair, and an orange kitten took a break next to the ball tower.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'minicat-chair.webp'} alt="A black cat lying on the seat of a white chair in a bright lounge." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A chair of his own.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'minicat-orange.webp'} alt="An orange kitten lying on a wood floor next to a purple ball-track toy." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>By the ball tower.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <RegionMap stores={BAY} region="Palo Alto" />

  <h2 id="brooklyn">Brooklyn Cat Cafe, New Year's Day 2023</h2>
  <p>
    On New Year's Day 2023, on a trip to New York, we stopped at <strong>Brooklyn
    Cat Cafe</strong> on Montague Street in Brooklyn Heights, a few blocks from the Promenade. One cat was asleep in a
    felt carrot on the counter, and a white cat lay upside down on a chair.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'brooklyn-carrot.webp'} alt="A black-and-white cat curled up asleep inside an orange felt carrot bed on a counter." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>In the carrot, Brooklyn Cat Cafe, January 1, 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'brooklyn-white-cat.webp'} alt="A white cat lying on its back on a chair seat, pawing at a hand." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Upside down on a chair.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    A black cat closed his eyes for a chin scratch, and a tuxedo cat kept watch over the street from the cat tree in the
    front window.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'brooklyn-black-cat.webp'} alt="A black cat with eyes closed, getting a chin scratch from a hand with an entry sticker." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A chin scratch.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'brooklyn-tuxedo.webp'} alt="A black-and-white cat lying on a cat tree platform by the front window." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>In the front window.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <RegionMap stores={AWAY} region="New York" />

  <h2 id="places">Cats that come with the place</h2>
  <p>
    Some places just have cats. At the <strong>Ernest Hemingway Home</strong> in Key West, on the 2024 road trip, the
    descendants of Hemingway's six-toed cat have the run of the house and garden. One was minding the gift shop
    counter, and an orange one patrolled the garden path. (More of them in
    <a href="/misc/roadtrip-2024">the road trip post</a>.)
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'hemingway-shop-cat.webp'} alt="A tortoiseshell cat standing on a white counter in the museum gift shop, next to a card reader." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Minding the shop, Hemingway Home, August 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'hemingway-orange-cat.webp'} alt="An orange cat walking across a gravel garden path edged with coral stones." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On patrol in the garden.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The biggest surprise came on the Big Island in September 2026. Driving into the self-parking lot of the Hilton Waikoloa Village
    after dark, we suddenly found the headlights full of cats: dozens of them, spread across the asphalt between the
    painted lines, a feral colony at its dinner hour. We had never heard of it, and spent ten minutes just watching.
    (The full story is in <a href="/misc/hawaii-2026">the Hawaiʻi post</a>.)
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'waikoloa-lot.webp'} alt="Cats of every color scattered across a dark parking lot at night, casting long shadows in the lights." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The cat parking lot, Waikoloa, September 9, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'waikoloa-calico.webp'} alt="A calico, a tabby-and-white and a white cat close up on the asphalt at night." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Up close.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <RegionMap stores={PLACES} region="Key West and Hawaiʻi" />

  <h2 id="fosters">Fosters, 2023</h2>
  <p>
    In 2023 the cats came to us for a change: we fostered three rounds of kittens. The first was a litter of orange and
    tabby kittens, with us from mid-May into early June. One of the orange ones decided a flowerpot was a bed.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'foster-box.webp'} alt="Four kittens, orange, tabby and tabby-and-white, piled together on a patterned blanket in a cardboard box." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The May litter, in their box.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'foster-pot.webp'} alt="An orange kitten sitting inside a white flowerpot, looking up at the camera." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Potted.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In September came a week of gray-and-white kittens, with a calico among them.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'foster-mat.webp'} alt="Two gray-and-white kittens curled up together on a white mat." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The September pair, day one.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'foster-sofa.webp'} alt="Two gray-and-white kittens playing on a tan leather sofa." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On the sofa.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And in December, one black-and-white kitten.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'foster-tuxedo.webp'} alt="A black-and-white kitten with white paws held in the crook of an arm in a pink sweater." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>December.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="away">On the road</h2>
  <p>
    And three more that are in the trip posts: a cat café in Richmond, BC (<a href="/misc/vancouver-2023">Vancouver,
    2023</a>), Tropicats in Līhuʻe (<a href="/misc/kauai-2026">Kauaʻi, 2026</a>) and Cat Café MOFF in Honolulu
    (<a href="/misc/hawaii-2026">Hawaiʻi, 2026</a>).
  </p>

  <p class="muted"><small>Photo locations have been removed from the published images. Visit counts come from our own
    records and only count the times we paid by card.</small></p>
  <Comments />
</BaseLayout>
